## Simple maze (simple-maze), generated from the Rosie teaching script (english-input.txt) under the world conventions.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##   4. The name of an action is block-step.
##   5. If a blue block is adjacent to a clear location then you can move the block onto the location.
##   6. If a location is not below an object then it is clear.
##   7. If a location is next to an object but it is not diagonal with the object then it is adjacent to the object.
##  11. The goal is that a blue block is on a blue location.
## World: init-mazerc.world (a grid of locations; the blue block, black blocks)
##
## Translation (tools/rosie-language.md gives the general reading; the assumption ledger is in README.md):
##   - Operator block-step (argument1 = the blue block, argument2 = the clear location), statement 5; adjacent (statement 7)
##     is a static relation between locations (A-G1); clear is a maintained one-argument relation (statement 6). The black
##     blocks are walls only in that they stand on locations, which are then not clear.
##   - The goal: a blue block is on a blue location.
## Matching hints for learned rules (World-Conventions L3-095, L11-009): many-valued attributes, sized from the initial world.
production optimize-attribute location 17
production optimize-attribute block 17
production optimize-attribute task 17
production optimize-attribute object 17
production optimize-attribute on 4
production optimize-attribute below 4
production optimize-attribute clear 12
production optimize-attribute adjacent 34


## Propose initialize-simple-maze when its conditions below hold.
sp {simple-maze*propose*initialize-simple-maze
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-simple-maze ^task-operator false)
}

